    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105411" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῐχ-ίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρίξ</span>) a kind
		of <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>anchovy full of small
				hair-like bones,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				551
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Eq.</u>
				662
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριχίδας ὠψώνησ᾽ ἅπαξ,</span>
			as a mark of a most thrifty person, <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				154
			</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				569b25
			</span></i>, and 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριχίας</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>.</div>
